{
  "pmid": "30170128",
  "instructions_version": "extract_v2",
  "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
  "relevance_note": "A narrative review of 2017 PID literature whose only individual-level TNFAIP3 content is one previously published patient: 'By using WES in an infant with lymphadenopathy, splenomegaly and persistent fever, Takagi et al.^37 found a biallelic mutation in the TNFAIP3 (HA20) gene'.",
  "method_note": "Read the whole paper (text and reference list; it has no tables in the Markdown). Rows were written by hand in a short Python script and every span was checked verbatim against the paper by script. Scope: only TNFAIP3-related individuals were extracted; people with other diseases summarized in the review (LAD, HYOU1, APDS etc.) were not. Group-level TNFAIP3 statements produced no rows: Zhou et al. 'six unrelated families' (no individuals, no variants), and the cohort studies ^38,39 (spectrum of manifestations only). The one individual ('an infant', from Takagi et al.^37) has no variant string; the variant row records the prose description. 'biallelic' cannot be mapped to homozygous vs compound heterozygous, so zygosity is 'not reported'; 'predicting a truncated protein' does not give a class, so variant_type is 'not reported'. 'persistent fever' was not mapped to the checklist item 'recurrent fever' (persistent is not recurrent). Age at diagnosis 'an infant' is taken from 'By using WES in an infant' (WES found the mutation). cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is true because the infant is attributed to Takagi et al.^37. Possible contradictions/inconsistencies in the paper: (1) the text cites 'Zhou et al.^36', but reference [36.] is Guo L et al. (EXTL3), so Zhou et al. has no matching reference entry; (2) the text says 'a biallelic mutation' for the Takagi infant, while reference [37.] is titled 'Haploinsufficiency of TNFAIP3 (A20) by germline mutation...'; recorded as printed in the text.",
